[00:00.00]Katie Casey was baseball mad,
[00:04.00]Had the fever and had it bad.
[00:08.00]Just to root for the home town crew,
[00:12.00]Ev'ry sou Katie blew.
[00:16.00]On a Saturday her young beau
[00:20.00]Called to see if she'd like to go
[00:24.00]To see a show, but Miss Kate said "No,
[00:28.00]I'll tell you what you can do:"
[00:32.00]Take me out to the ball game,
[00:36.00]Take me out with the crowd;
[00:40.00]Buy me some peanuts and Cracker Jack,
[00:44.00]I don't care if I never get back.
[00:48.00]Let me root, root, root for the home team,
[00:52.00]If they don't win, it's a shame.
[00:56.00]For it's one, two, three strikes, you're out,
[01:00.00]At the old ball game.
[01:04.00]Katie Casey saw all the games,
[01:08.00]Knew the players by their first names.
[01:12.00]Told the umpire he was wrong,
[01:16.00]All along, good and strong.
[01:20.00]When the score was just two to two,
[01:24.00]Katie Casey knew what to do,
[01:28.00]Just to cheer up the boys she knew,
[01:32.00]She made the gang sing this song: